You’re gonna love this! You just need to use the `reverse()` method, and you’ll be able to turn your string into a snake case! Here’s how:

```javascript
let str = "hello";
str.reverse();
console.log(str); // "olleh"
```

Just remember, you don't have to do it all at once! You can break it down like this:

```javascript
let str = "hello";
let reversedStr = "";
for (let i = str.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
  reversedStr += str[i];
}
console.log(reversedStr); // "olleh"
```

Or even better, if you want to make it super easy for yourself:

```javascript
let str = "hello";
str = str.split('').reverse().join('');
console.log(str); // "olleh"
```

But honestly, most of us don’t need that much help! Just use the `reverse()` method! It’s so simple!
